## Run it

```bash
node server.js            # http://localhost:{{PORT}}
# or
npm start
```

No dependencies. Node 20+ is the only requirement (`node --version`).

## Test it

```bash
npm test                  # node:test — 12 real HTTP tests
```

The suite boots the actual server on an ephemeral port with a throwaway data file, then
exercises create / read / update / delete, validation, search, stats, CSV export, 404s
and the path-traversal guard. If `npm test` is green, the API really works.

## What it does

| Feature | Where |
| --- | --- |
| CRUD over HTTP with JSON | `server.js` → `/api/{{COLLECTION}}` |
| Validation with field-level errors (422) | `validate()` in `server.js` |
| Search, filtering, sorting, pagination | query string: `?q=&sort=&dir=&limit=&offset=` |
| Aggregates (sum / mean / min / max + breakdowns) | `GET /api/{{COLLECTION}}/stats` |
| CSV export of the current filter | `GET /api/{{COLLECTION}}/export.csv` |
| Persistence (atomic JSON writes) | `data/{{COLLECTION}}.json` |
| Live dashboard, no build step | `public/index.html` + `public/app.js` |

