## API

```
GET    /api/health                     → { status, collection, records }
GET    /api/{{COLLECTION}}                   → { total, limit, offset, items }
POST   /api/{{COLLECTION}}                   → 201 created record
GET    /api/{{COLLECTION}}/:id               → single record
PATCH  /api/{{COLLECTION}}/:id               → partial update
PUT    /api/{{COLLECTION}}/:id               → full update
DELETE /api/{{COLLECTION}}/:id               → { deleted: id }
GET    /api/{{COLLECTION}}/stats             → aggregates
GET    /api/{{COLLECTION}}/export.csv        → CSV of the filtered set
```

```bash
curl -X POST localhost:{{PORT}}/api/{{COLLECTION}} \
  -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  -d '{{CURL_EXAMPLE}}'
```

## Deployment

The server binds `0.0.0.0:$PORT`, so any container host works as-is:

```dockerfile
FROM node:22-alpine
WORKDIR /app
COPY . .
ENV PORT=3000
CMD ["node", "server.js"]
```

